  [PASS] V3 (THE SELECTION ATTACK DOES NOT LAND, AND I RECORD THAT IT DOES NOT) I expected g05's four to be the extreme tail of their own population -- they are, after all, exactly the four the MOND literature has flagged for twenty years (Baumgardt et al. 2005, ApJ 634, 1093; Ibata et al. 2011, ApJ 738, 186; Sanders 2012, MNRAS 419, L6).  They are not.  Expanding to every catalogue cluster meeting answer-blind criteria, on measured dispersions, 17 of 20 are still negative and the sixteen clusters g05 did NOT use sit within a tenth of a dex of the four it did.  The class-level statement is real; only the -0.859 magnitude is not, and that is V2's doing, not selection   (N = 20 clusters, 17 negative (85 per cent), median -0.408 dex, range -0.925 to +0.229.  g05's four inside this pool: median -0.505; the 16 it did not use: median -0.408; difference -0.097 dex)

==========================================================================================================================
V4.  THE MASS-TO-LIGHT DECOMPOSITION.  How much of the residual is the kernel and how much is Upsilon_V = 2?
==========================================================================================================================
  g_obs/g_pred = [g_obs / g_Newt(Ups_V L)] x [1/boost].  The first bracket is a purely NEWTONIAN statement --
  log10 of the dynamical-to-assumed-photometric mass ratio -- and says nothing about this framework.  Only the
  second is the kernel's prediction.  If the first carried most of the residual, the claim would be about M/L.
  cluster      g05 dex  log10 boost  Newt part  M/L needed  Baumgardt M/L_V
  Pal 4         -0.874        0.658     -0.216        1.22             0.81
  Pal 14        -1.306        0.812     -0.494        0.64             1.70
  Pal 3         -0.844        0.812     -0.033        1.86             1.45
  NGC 2419      -0.211        0.190     -0.021        1.90             1.61
  [PASS] V4 (THE ATTACK DOES NOT LAND) I expected the assumed Upsilon_V = 2 to be carrying most of the cluster deficit, because these mass-segregated outer-halo clusters have low dynamical M/L.  It is not: the Newtonian M/L part is a small minority of the residual and the kernel's own boost carries the great majority of it.  This attack fails and I record that it fails -- to the extent the clusters ARE below the kernel, it is the kernel doing it   (median Newtonian M/L part -0.124 dex against median kernel-boost part +0.735 dex, i.e. the M/L assumption is 14 per cent of the quoted -0.859.  Upsilon_V these clusters would need under Newton: Pal 4 1.22, Pal 14 0.64, Pal 3 1.86, NGC 2419 1.90)
  
  The Upsilon_V scan, on g05's own dispersions, since Upsilon_V is the only free knob on the cluster side:
   Upsilon_V      Pal 4     Pal 14      Pal 3   NGC 2419    median
         0.8     -0.648     -0.912     -0.577     +0.059    -0.612
         1.0     -0.704     -1.008     -0.652     -0.004    -0.678
         1.5     -0.804     -1.183     -0.769     -0.123    -0.786
         2.0     -0.874     -1.306     -0.844     -0.211    -0.859
         3.0     -0.975     -1.474     -0.946     -0.341    -0.960
  [FAIL] V4b g05's own Upsilon_V = 1 caveat is an ASSERTED number where a computed one belongs, and it is wrong -- though wrong AGAINST g05's own point.  g05 shifted the median by log10(2) = 0.301, which is the NEWTONIAN response to halving the mass; three of its four clusters are in the modified regime where the response is smaller.  The correctly recomputed Upsilon_V = 1 median is more negative than g05 claims, not less   (g05 asserts -0.558 at Upsilon_V = 1; recomputed it is -0.678.  Full scan: Ups=0.8: -0.612, Ups=1.0: -0.678, Ups=1.5: -0.786, Ups=2.0: -0.859, Ups=3.0: -0.960)

