     exact permutation over all C(16,4) = 1820 label assignments:
        on g05's dispersions:      separation -0.973 dex, p = 0.0033
        on MEASURED dispersions:   separation -0.630 dex, p = 0.0099
  [PASS] V5b (THE SIGN SURVIVES THE DISPERSION SWAP, EVEN THOUGH THE SIZE DOES NOT) with the measured dispersions the separation shrinks by more than half a dex, but the clusters still sit below the dwarfs and the exact permutation test still rejects at the two-sigma level.  So the DIRECTION of g05's S5 survives V2 even though its magnitude does not   (g05 dispersions: -0.973 dex, p = 0.0033.  Measured dispersions: -0.630 dex, p = 0.0099 over 1820 exact assignments)

==========================================================================================================================
V6.  THE DISCRIMINANT.  Is it DARK-MATTER CONTENT, or one of several perfectly degenerate labels?
==========================================================================================================================
  The claim is not merely 'clusters sit below'.  It is that the SIGN is predicted by DARK-MATTER CONTENT rather
  than by support type.  For that to be a discriminant, dark-matter content must be identified against every
  other variable that separates the two classes.  It is not.
     baryonic mass: 2.37 dex apart, 0 of 12 dwarfs overlapping the cluster range
     physical size: 1.13 dex apart, 0 of 12 dwarfs overlapping the cluster range
  [FAIL] V6a (THE ATTACK LANDS) at matched internal acceleration the two classes are ALSO separated by more than two decades in baryonic mass and more than one in physical size, with ZERO overlap in either.  'Dark-matter content', 'baryonic mass' and 'physical size' are three names for the same partition of these sixteen objects.  A two-class comparison cannot tell them apart, so naming dark matter as THE predictor is a choice and not a measurement -- a kernel that failed as a function of system size or of baryonic mass, which would be a framework LIABILITY rather than a vindication of dark matter, fits this data exactly as well   (baryonic-mass separation 2.37 dex with 0/12 overlap; size separation 1.13 dex with 0/12 overlap.  Two classes, three degenerate candidate predictors, no power to separate them)
  
  And the dark-matter variable is not independent on the dwarf side: a dwarf's dark-matter content is measured
  as M_dyn/M_bar with M_dyn = 3 sigma^2 r_1/2 / G -- the SAME sigma and r_1/2 that build the residual.
  [FAIL] V6b (THE ATTACK LANDS) inside the dwarf sample the residual and the dark-matter fraction are two monotone functions of one number: M_dyn is built from the very sigma and r_1/2 that build the residual.  They correlate at r = 0.95 BY CONSTRUCTION, not by physics.  'Dark-matter content predicts the residual' is therefore near-tautological wherever dark-matter content is inferred dynamically.  The only non-circular half of the claim is the cluster side, where 'no dark matter' is a structure-formation statement rather than a dynamical inference   (log10(M_dyn/M_bar) against residual on the 12 matched dwarfs: r = +0.946, slope +0.535 dex per dex)

==========================================================================================================================
V7.  BOTH FOOTINGS, AND THE MUTATION CONTROLS.
==========================================================================================================================
     canonical  a_0=9.36e-11:  clusters(g05 sigma) -0.859   clusters(measured sigma) -0.516   dwarfs +0.114 (N=12)
     alt        a_0=1.13e-10:  clusters(g05 sigma) -0.896   clusters(measured sigma) -0.547   dwarfs -0.007 (N=11)
  [PASS] V7 both a_0 footings tell the same story, in both directions: g05's headline is footing-independent, and so is the fact that it halves when the measured dispersions replace the model ones.  a_0 is not the issue here   (canonical: g05 -0.859, measured -0.516, dwarfs +0.114; alt: g05 -0.896, measured -0.547, dwarfs -0.007)
  [PASS] M1 MUTATION CONTROL: with the kernel switched off the cluster residual must reduce EXACTLY to the Newtonian dynamical-to-photometric mass ratio computed independently, so V4's decomposition is arithmetic and not a story   (max discrepancy 1.665e-16 dex)
  [PASS] M2 MUTATION CONTROL on the data: inflating every observed dispersion by sqrt(10) must move every residual by exactly +1.000 dex and nothing else in the pipeline may respond   (shifts +1.000000000, +1.000000000, +1.000000000, +1.000000000)
  [PASS] M3 MUTATION CONTROL on the claim: if the clusters sat ON the kernel instead of below it, the same exact permutation test must stop rejecting.  It does, so V5b is testing the data and not the machinery   (clusters forced to 0.000 dex: separation -0.114 dex, exact p = 0.3764, against p = 0.0099 for the measured-dispersion data and p = 0.0033 for g05's)

==========================================================================================================================
VERDICT ON THE CLAIM
==========================================================================================================================
  THE DIRECTION SURVIVES.  THE NUMBER DOES NOT, AND NEITHER DOES THE WORD 'DARK MATTER'.

  WHAT SURVIVED EVERY ATTACK I COULD MOUNT:
   * The four clusters are faithful to the on-disk catalogue: worst residual difference 0.0005 dex (V1).
   * The acceleration match is real -- three of four clusters lie inside the dwarfs' own x_i range (V5a).
   * Even after every correction below, the clusters still sit BELOW the dwarfs at matched x_i, -0.630 dex,
     exact permutation p = 0.0099 (V5b), on both a_0 footings (V7).
   * The deficit is NOT a stellar mass-to-light artefact.  I expected it to be and it is not: the Newtonian M/L
     part is -0.124 dex against a kernel-boost part of +0.735 dex (V4).  That attack failed.
   * It is NOT a cherry-pick either, and I expected it to be.  Every one of the 20 catalogue clusters meeting
     answer-blind criteria on measured dispersions: 17 of 20 negative, class median -0.408 dex, and the
     16 clusters g05 did not use sit at -0.408 against -0.505 for the four it did (V3).  That attack failed too.
  So the FIRST sentence of the claim -- 'support type does not predict the sign of the residual' -- STANDS, and
  it stands at the CLASS level, not just on four objects: -0.41 dex on 20 clusters against +0.11 on 12 dwarfs.

  WHAT DID NOT SURVIVE:
   1. THE NUMBER.  -0.859 dex is not the measurement.  Two of g05's four dispersions are taken from the sigma0
      column of the Baumgardt PARAMETER table, which is the central dispersion of a fitted NEWTONIAN N-body
      model -- a quantity derived under the theory being tested.  The MEASURED profiles are in this repository
      (baumgardt_gc_veldisp_profiles.tsv, header: 'These are the DATA, not model curves').  Using the measured
      dispersion at each cluster's half-light radius the median goes -0.859 -> -0.516 dex.  Pal 3 moves
      +0.655 dex on its own: measured 1.70 km/s from 22 stars where g05 used the model's 0.80.
      Pal 14 moves +0.543: Baumgardt's compilation of the SAME stars Jordi et al. measured gives 0.71,
      not 0.38.  g05's own weakest-link statement flagged the Pal 14 discrepancy and then used the small value
      anyway; it did not flag that Pal 3's number is a model output at all.
   2. THE MAGNITUDE AGAIN, INDEPENDENTLY.  The full answer-blind class of 20 clusters gives -0.408 dex, not
      -0.859.  Two independent routes -- swapping the model dispersions for measured ones on g05's own four, and
      expanding to the whole class -- both land near -0.4 to -0.5 dex.  '-0.859' should be retired (V2, V3).
   3. THE DISCRIMINANT IS NOT IDENTIFIED.  At matched x_i the classes are also 2.37 dex apart in baryonic mass
      (0/12 overlap) and 1.13 dex apart in size (0/12 overlap).  'Dark-matter content', 'baryonic mass'
      and 'physical size' name the SAME partition of these sixteen objects.  A kernel that fails as a function
      of size or mass -- a framework liability, NOT a vindication of dark matter -- predicts this data equally
      well.  Two classes cannot separate three degenerate labels (V6a).
   4. AND ON THE DWARF SIDE THE DARK-MATTER VARIABLE IS CIRCULAR.  M_dyn = 3 sigma^2 r_1/2 / G is built from the
      same sigma and r_1/2 as the residual: r = +0.946 by construction (V6b).  Only the cluster side's 'no dark
      matter' is an independent statement, so the claim rests on one non-circular half.
   5. A SMALL ONE, AGAINST g05'S OWN INTEREST.  Its Upsilon_V = 1 caveat, -0.558 dex, is asserted by adding
      log10(2) -- the NEWTONIAN response -- when three of four clusters are in the modified regime.  Recomputed
      it is -0.678 dex (V4b).

  WHAT MAY BE QUOTED AFTER THIS FILE:
   * 'Globular clusters, equally pressure-supported, sit BELOW the framework's kernel where dwarf spheroidals at
     the same internal acceleration sit above it -- -0.63 dex on g05's four with measured dispersions (exact
     permutation p = 0.01), and -0.41 dex on the full answer-blind class of 20.  Support type does
     not predict the sign of the residual.'
   * That MOND over-predicts outer-halo cluster dispersions is long known (Baumgardt et al. 2005; Ibata et al.
     2011; Sanders 2012); nothing here is new except the branch-free prescription.
  NOT: '-0.859 dex' or 'median -0.859'.  It is inflated by two model dispersions; both independent routes give
  about -0.41 to -0.52 dex.
  NOT: '...dark-matter content does.'  That is one of at least three degenerate readings of a two-class
  comparison, and the dark-matter variable is not independently measured on the side carrying the weight.

RESULT: 13 checks, 4 FAIL -> ["V2 (THE ATTACK LANDS, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS) g05's four dispersions are a MIXTURE of literature values and two entries from the sigma0 column of the Baumgardt parameter table, which is a fitted NEWTONIAN N-body model's central dispersion.  Replacing all four with the MEASURED dispersion at the half-light radius, from the measured-profile file already sitting in this repository, moves the median by more than half a dex.  Pal 3 alone moves by +0.65 dex: its measured dispersion is 1.70 km/s from 22 stars where g05 used the model's 0.80.  Pal 14 moves by +0.53: Baumgardt's compilation of the SAME stars Jordi et al. measured gives 0.71, not 0.38.  A headline number that halves when you swap a model output for the measurement it was fitted to is not a measured number", "V4b g05's own Upsilon_V = 1 caveat is an ASSERTED number where a computed one belongs, and it is wrong -- though wrong AGAINST g05's own point.  g05 shifted the median by log10(2) = 0.301, which is the NEWTONIAN response to halving the mass; three of its four clusters are in the modified regime where the response is smaller.  The correctly recomputed Upsilon_V = 1 median is more negative than g05 claims, not less", "V6a (THE ATTACK LANDS) at matched internal acceleration the two classes are ALSO separated by more than two decades in baryonic mass and more than one in physical size, with ZERO overlap in either.  'Dark-matter content', 'baryonic mass' and 'physical size' are three names for the same partition of these sixteen objects.  A two-class comparison cannot tell them apart, so naming dark matter as THE predictor is a choice and not a measurement -- a kernel that failed as a function of system size or of baryonic mass, which would be a framework LIABILITY rather than a vindication of dark matter, fits this data exactly as well", "V6b (THE ATTACK LANDS) inside the dwarf sample the residual and the dark-matter fraction are two monotone functions of one number: M_dyn is built from the very sigma and r_1/2 that build the residual.  They correlate at r = 0.95 BY CONSTRUCTION, not by physics.  'Dark-matter content predicts the residual' is therefore near-tautological wherever dark-matter content is inferred dynamically.  The only non-circular half of the claim is the cluster side, where 'no dark matter' is a structure-formation statement rather than a dynamical inference"]   rc=1
